-- CK-39: an imported record alias's implicit constructor builds the RECORD,
-- as in Elm (language.md §0; checker-v2.md §14.2, the record-alias
-- constructor rows; D12 for its representation). `P 1 "a"` is a
-- `{ x : Int, y : String }`, so `.y` reads `"a"`. Expected `a`.
--
-- Oracle twin, run on 7427828: this project with `p = { x = 1, y = "a" }`
-- in place of the constructor call prints `a`. As written, 7427828 refuses
-- it with TYPE MISMATCH "This is not a record with a `y` field: It is: `P`"
-- — `Schemes.instantiateCtor` types every imported constructor as a nominal.
import Node exposing (Program)
import Pt exposing (P)


p =
    P 1 "a"


main : Program
main =
    Node.printLines [ p.y ]
